<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4499" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Augustānus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Augustīānus</span></b> , Suet Ner 25; Front. Col.
		pp. 1, 106, 139 Goes.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Augustānĕus</span></b> , Auct. Limit. p. 265
		Goes.), a, um, adj.
		Augustus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>pertaining to
			Augustus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					50, 15, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">DOMVS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2350</span></i>
			 and 2947.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to an
			emperor</i>, <i>imperial</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Augustani,</span>”
				<i>Roman knights appointed by Nero</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner.
			25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Augustāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of cities which had the title Augusta</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3, 4, § 23
		al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
